# Oracle Cloud Worker Configuration Template
# =============================================
#
# This file contains the IP addresses or hostnames of your Oracle Cloud
# ARM compute instances that will serve as ULTRATHINK workers.
#
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS:
# 1. Run the provisioning script to create Oracle Cloud VMs:
#    cd ../setup
#    python3 provision_oracle_vms.py
#
# 2. After provisioning, copy this file to workers.txt:
#    cp workers.txt.template workers.txt
#
# 3. Replace the example IPs below with your actual VM public IPs
#    (shown after provisioning completes)
#
# FORMAT:
# - One IP address or hostname per line
# - No quotes or additional formatting
# - Comments (lines starting with #) are ignored
#
# EXAMPLE ENTRIES:
# 129.153.123.456
# 129.153.234.567
# 129.153.345.678
# 129.153.456.789
#
# Or if you've set up DNS:
# worker1.example.com
# worker2.example.com
# worker3.example.com
# worker4.example.com
#
# IMPORTANT:
# - Ensure SSH access is configured for all workers
# - Workers must be accessible on port 22 (SSH) and 8000 (API)
# - Run ./check_workers.sh after deployment to verify connectivity
#
# =============================================
# ADD YOUR WORKER IPs BELOW (4 workers total)
# =============================================